00:16:36.572 --> 00:16:38.118
'cause you've got such a wide range.

00:16:38.118 --> 00:16:40.328
And I feel like it would be a good place

00:16:40.328 --> 00:16:41.662
to build up your portfolio

00:16:41.662 --> 00:16:44.162
because from what I see, like,

00:16:45.349 --> 00:16:46.392
it doesn't really matter

00:16:46.392 --> 00:16:48.548
where you had your education or whatever.

00:16:48.548 --> 00:16:50.198
What we really care about

00:16:50.198 --> 00:16:52.465
'cause most of the time
we are the clients now.

00:16:52.465 --> 00:16:53.505
We're buying the service.

00:16:53.505 --> 00:16:55.313
We just care about your portfolio.

00:16:55.313 --> 00:16:57.014
That's the thing that's
most important to me.

00:16:57.014 --> 00:16:57.847
- Yeah, exactly.

00:16:57.847 --> 00:16:59.055
I'm like, show me your work.

00:16:59.055 --> 00:17:00.936
- It's a good place to build
up your portfolio as well

00:17:00.936 --> 00:17:01.974
and also get paid.

00:17:01.974 --> 00:17:03.182
- Yeah.

00:17:03.182 --> 00:17:05.391
I mean, I used to recommend
to voice actors, you know,

00:17:05.391 --> 00:17:07.864
if no one's hiring you, you
don't know where to start,

00:17:07.864 --> 00:17:09.272
you know, don't go to
one of these websites

00:17:09.272 --> 00:17:12.105
that costs, like, $400
a year to sign up too

00:17:12.105 --> 00:17:13.471
'cause you're not gonna
make your money back.

00:17:13.471 --> 00:17:14.340
- Yeah, like for example,

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.238
if we're hiring video editors,

00:17:16.238 --> 00:17:17.988
like we can get emails about people

00:17:17.988 --> 00:17:21.146
who are qualified for X, Y, and Z.

00:17:21.146 --> 00:17:22.420
But at the end of the day,

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.634
we're most likely gonna pick people

00:17:24.634 --> 00:17:26.369
who have worked on anime videos

00:17:26.369 --> 00:17:28.608
'cause we know they
have experience working

00:17:28.608 --> 00:17:29.680
in that fuckin' field.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.002
- Or who, like, actually know us

00:17:31.002 --> 00:17:33.360
and, like, watch our videos and stuff.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.193
- Yeah, exactly.

00:17:34.193 --> 00:17:35.707
So, that's the thing.

00:17:35.707 --> 00:17:39.578
It's more about knowing
your target audience

00:17:39.578 --> 00:17:41.729
and knowing what your
personal branding is.

00:17:41.729 --> 00:17:44.227
And it's less important
about what you put on your CV

00:17:44.227 --> 00:17:47.044
because we don't really
care about CVs that much.

00:17:47.044 --> 00:17:48.601
- I don't give a shit
what school you went to.

00:17:48.601 --> 00:17:49.654
Is the shit good or not?

00:17:49.654 --> 00:17:51.122
Like, it's all there is to it.

00:17:51.122 --> 00:17:53.085
- There's lots of video editors out there.

00:17:53.085 --> 00:17:54.742
It's just a matter of-

00:17:54.742 --> 00:17:56.614
- I normally go to,
like, Fiverr or somewhere

00:17:56.614 --> 00:17:59.657
for like if I need something,
like, one off and, like, fast.

00:17:59.657 --> 00:18:01.639
Like, I just like, because other times

00:18:01.639 --> 00:18:03.054
it's a bit of a pain to search around.

00:18:03.054 --> 00:18:06.122
- Have you used Fiverr other
than in your Fiverr videos?

00:18:06.122 --> 00:18:07.000
- Yeah, I've used it.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.833
I used it for, where did I use it?

00:18:10.964 --> 00:18:12.830
If I need something composed.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.710
'Cause I don't know any composers.

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:15.922
Like, making music.

00:18:15.922 --> 00:18:19.272
- I go from knowing zero
composers to Kevin Penkin.

00:18:19.272 --> 00:18:21.594
(everyone laughs)

00:18:21.594 --> 00:18:22.761
- I can't go, "Oh, Kevin mate.

00:18:22.761 --> 00:18:24.103
"I got this video idea.

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:27.078
"Could you just compose
me a track for it?"

00:18:27.078 --> 00:18:28.195
Like, so I'll go to someone I'm like,

00:18:28.195 --> 00:18:30.979
I'm only like make it,
like, a middy track of this

00:18:30.979 --> 00:18:32.928
or make, like, a version of that.

00:18:32.928 --> 00:18:34.787
It's normally very basic, like, thing

00:18:34.787 --> 00:18:37.122
where I'm, like, "Copy this thing."

00:18:37.122 --> 00:18:39.072
Yeah, I mean, I think I've had, like,

00:18:39.072 --> 00:18:41.696
some emotes on my Twitch drawn there.

00:18:41.696 --> 00:18:42.529
It was pretty decent.

00:18:42.529 --> 00:18:44.608
Yeah, there's a lot of
Twitch stuff on there.

00:18:44.608 --> 00:18:46.368
- I mean, there's a lot of
artists on Fiverr, right?

00:18:46.368 --> 00:18:49.163
- Yeah, oh my god, there's so many.

00:18:49.163 --> 00:18:50.811
- Or "artists."

00:18:50.811 --> 00:18:52.257
- Is that where you get your Twitch stuff?

00:18:52.257 --> 00:18:54.834
'Cause I've actually been looking to try

00:18:54.834 --> 00:18:57.118
and, like, upgrade my Twitch presentation

00:18:57.118 --> 00:18:59.535
because my Twitch
presentation is fuckin' shit

00:18:59.535 --> 00:19:01.892
because I've never given the
shit about streaming before.

00:19:01.892 --> 00:19:05.478
- Problem is on Fiverr,
it's tailored towards, like,

00:19:05.478 --> 00:19:08.130
I think what the like
general audience of people

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.996
who are looking to get into
live streaming would want.

00:19:09.996 --> 00:19:13.771
So it's all like very gamer looking.

00:19:13.771 --> 00:19:15.678
You know what I mean
when I say that, right?

00:19:15.678 --> 00:19:20.072
Like, 90% of the Fiverr
stuff for, like, Twitch,

00:19:20.072 --> 00:19:22.114
like, Twitch overlays
all looks like something

00:19:22.114 --> 00:19:24.324
that is an application to the FaZe Clan.

00:19:24.324 --> 00:19:26.194
Like, it doesn't look like-

00:19:26.194 --> 00:19:27.724
- It's like the default ones

00:19:27.724 --> 00:19:29.252
that you get on, like, Streamlabs, right?

00:19:29.252 --> 00:19:31.490
- Yeah, which is why I think
I ended up hiring someone

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:33.642
who I know that did a lot of this stuff

00:19:33.642 --> 00:19:35.093
and who watched some of my stuff.

00:19:35.093 --> 00:19:37.614
So they were kind of
familiar with my stuff.

00:19:37.614 --> 00:19:39.103
- I'm thinking to update mine as well.

00:19:39.103 --> 00:19:40.717
And I met an artist recently

00:19:40.717 --> 00:19:42.662
who probably gonna get to hire

00:19:42.662 --> 00:19:44.022
because yeah, at the same thing.

00:19:44.022 --> 00:19:46.109
Like, right now I'm using,
like, a default one.

00:19:46.109 --> 00:19:50.027
I'm just like, should probably
personalize it a little more,

00:19:50.027 --> 00:19:51.650
make it stand out a little bit.

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:53.440
- How'd you guys find artists?

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.305
You just DM people on Twitter?

00:19:55.305 --> 00:19:57.083
- I just tweet out or,
like, ask on live streams.

00:19:57.083 --> 00:19:58.569
I'm like, "Hey guys, I need something.

00:19:58.569 --> 00:20:00.530
"Can someone tell me like where I go?"

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.809
- A lot of them actually
I find through, like,

00:20:02.809 --> 00:20:04.174
them doing fan art of me.

00:20:04.174 --> 00:20:05.007
- Okay.

00:20:05.007 --> 00:20:07.702
- Yeah, so like the person I'm
probably gonna be hiring soon

00:20:07.702 --> 00:20:09.869
is Rocket Cat who did
like a bunch of, like,

00:20:09.869 --> 00:20:13.401
drawings with me and Chris,
the journey across Japan stuff.

00:20:13.401 --> 00:20:14.725
And it was really fuckin' cute.

00:20:14.725 --> 00:20:15.884
So I asked her and I was like,

00:20:15.884 --> 00:20:17.633
"Can you do some Twitch stuff?"

00:20:17.633 --> 00:20:18.503
And she was like, "Okay."

00:20:18.503 --> 00:20:19.972
So just asking around really.

00:20:19.972 --> 00:20:21.965
- I have, like, no idea what art is worth,

00:20:21.965 --> 00:20:23.382
so whatever they give me,
if it's not ridiculous.

00:20:23.382 --> 00:20:24.715
- Yeah, yeah.

00:20:24.715 --> 00:20:25.548
- Yeah, sure, fuck it.

00:20:25.548 --> 00:20:26.381
I'll pay that.

00:20:26.381 --> 00:20:28.935
- I'm way more comfortable
being like, "What do you want?"

00:20:28.935 --> 00:20:32.934
You know, versus like,
"I'll give you $15."

00:20:32.934 --> 00:20:34.521
- There's always a debate, right?

00:20:34.521 --> 00:20:37.313
Is it you as the buyer should ask

00:20:37.313 --> 00:20:39.941
or should the person, the client, say,

00:20:39.941 --> 00:20:41.071
"Hey, this is what I'm worth."

00:20:41.071 --> 00:20:42.937
Because it frustrates me when I hear like,

00:20:42.937 --> 00:20:43.804
"What's your budget?"

00:20:43.804 --> 00:20:45.374
And I'm like, I don't
have a fuckin' budget.

00:20:45.374 --> 00:20:47.410
- What are you worth?

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.669
- What's your hourly rate?

00:20:48.669 --> 00:20:49.502
You tell me.

00:20:49.502 --> 00:20:50.335
Like, I don't know

00:20:50.335 --> 00:20:51.702
I understand that that's in place

00:20:51.702 --> 00:20:54.103
for people who can't maybe
afford, like, a lot of things.

00:20:54.103 --> 00:20:55.022
But I'm like, "I don't know.

00:20:55.022 --> 00:20:56.653
"Whatever you think it's
worth, tell me, I'll pay it."

00:20:56.653 --> 00:20:58.225
- It's like a fuckin' standoff, right?

00:20:58.225 --> 00:21:00.304
It's like, you're
waiting for the first one

00:21:00.304 --> 00:21:01.382
to, like, say a number.

00:21:01.382 --> 00:21:03.630
It's just like, how much is this worth?

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:04.718
Like, what's your budget?

00:21:04.718 --> 00:21:06.968
I fuckin' hate that debate!

00:21:08.389 --> 00:21:09.976
- I get it from the artist's perspective

00:21:09.976 --> 00:21:11.218
because like, they're probably like,

00:21:11.218 --> 00:21:12.921
"Oh, if I say something
that's a little too high

00:21:12.921 --> 00:21:15.087
"then I'm afraid I might lose the client."

00:21:15.087 --> 00:21:15.920
- Right.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.190
That's when you can negotiate, right?

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.435
You can be like, "Ah, I think
that's a little too high."

00:21:19.435 --> 00:21:20.874
- Yeah, but a lot of them starting off

00:21:20.874 --> 00:21:21.822
don't know any better.

00:21:21.822 --> 00:21:22.655
- True, true.

00:21:22.655 --> 00:21:24.119
- I was afraid at first as well.

00:21:24.119 --> 00:21:25.988
Like, when you know, I'd get
sponsorship opportunities

00:21:25.988 --> 00:21:27.895
they'd be like, "What do you want for it?"

00:21:27.895 --> 00:21:29.130
I'm like, "Ah, fuck.

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:31.083
"I don't know.

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:32.299
"How much do you have?"

00:21:32.299 --> 00:21:35.783
- Have either you been ever
good at, like, bartering or?

00:21:35.783 --> 00:21:37.241
- I love doing it.

00:21:37.241 --> 00:21:38.602
- Like, I've learned to do it

00:21:38.602 --> 00:21:40.893
just 'cause my dad was really good at it.

00:21:40.893 --> 00:21:42.169
- I fuckin' suck at it, man.

00:21:42.169 --> 00:21:43.614
This is why I love Japan

00:21:43.614 --> 00:21:46.006
where everything is labeled and priced.

00:21:46.006 --> 00:21:47.570
Because whenever I go to Thailand,

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:51.250
you just play this dance
around everything you buy, man.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:54.079
Because it is a fuckin'
dance where you're just like,

00:21:54.079 --> 00:21:56.908
"Oh, okay, so you're gonna charge me that?

00:21:56.908 --> 00:21:59.910
"Well, I'm gonna, like, say a
price that's 10 times lower."

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:02.210
- In Australia it's, like, a
dance that you will only dance

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.900
if you decide to enter the ring.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:04.947
(everyone laughs)

00:22:04.947 --> 00:22:07.108
It's like, you can stand back
and just kind of be like,

00:22:07.108 --> 00:22:07.982
"Oh, this is how much you want?

00:22:07.982 --> 00:22:08.815
"All right then."

00:22:08.815 --> 00:22:09.648
Pull your wallet out.

00:22:09.648 --> 00:22:10.481
But then you could also be like,

00:22:10.481 --> 00:22:12.277
"Hold on, let me roll up
my sleeves real quick.

00:22:12.277 --> 00:22:14.267
"Let's samba, baby."

00:22:14.267 --> 00:22:16.293
Because like my dad was so fuckin',

00:22:16.293 --> 00:22:18.642
'cause my dad has been,
like, an IT salesman

00:22:18.642 --> 00:22:20.020
for, like, the past 30 years.

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:21.721
So this man, I don't know
how the fuck he did it,

00:22:21.721 --> 00:22:25.619
but I remember, like, when
I was in, like, high school

00:22:25.619 --> 00:22:28.368
or something and I wanted
to buy my first guitar,

00:22:28.368 --> 00:22:30.266
like a proper electric guitar.

00:22:30.266 --> 00:22:32.915
And he bought me like this like
really nice Epiphone guitar

00:22:32.915 --> 00:22:34.935
which is worth like
two grand or something.

00:22:34.935 --> 00:22:36.568
And he looked at it and he's like,

00:22:36.568 --> 00:22:38.270
"So this is just the guitar, right?"

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:39.103
And the guy's like, "Yeah."

00:22:39.103 --> 00:22:41.498
He was like, "Can I have
a chat with you, mate?"

00:22:41.498 --> 00:22:45.719
And he took the dude back
behind the counter into a room.

00:22:45.719 --> 00:22:46.861
And he's like, "Hold on, son."

00:22:46.861 --> 00:22:47.919
- Did he fuckin' beat him up?

00:22:47.919 --> 00:22:49.002
- I don't know!

00:22:49.002 --> 00:22:50.738
- Why'd he have to go in the back?

00:22:50.738 --> 00:22:51.991
Why couldn't he do it at the counter?

00:22:51.991 --> 00:22:52.824
- I don't know.

00:22:52.824 --> 00:22:53.657
I don't know.

00:22:53.657 --> 00:22:54.490
But he like took him to the back.

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:55.323
He was like, "All right, let me talk."

00:22:55.323 --> 00:22:58.912
And then I think maybe like
10 minutes later he came out.

00:22:58.912 --> 00:22:59.745
- It's free.

00:22:59.745 --> 00:23:00.578
It's free.

00:23:00.578 --> 00:23:02.161
(everyone laughs)

00:23:02.161 --> 00:23:03.322
- Black eye.

00:23:03.322 --> 00:23:04.774
(everyone laughs)

00:23:04.774 --> 00:23:05.851
- He came out 10 minutes later,

00:23:05.851 --> 00:23:08.703
and he's like, "All right,
so the guitar now is 1500."

00:23:08.703 --> 00:23:09.772
And he threw in a free amp.

00:23:09.772 --> 00:23:12.831
And I'm like, "What did you say?

00:23:12.831 --> 00:23:14.131
"What did you do?

00:23:14.131 --> 00:23:14.964
"How did you do it?"

00:23:14.964 --> 00:23:16.095
He's like, "I just talked to him, mate."

00:23:16.095 --> 00:23:17.914
I'm like, no, no, no, no, no.

00:23:17.914 --> 00:23:19.398
Like, if it was that easy,

00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:21.491
then everyone would be getting deals.

00:23:21.491 --> 00:23:24.248
It's not just a matter of,
"Oh, I just talked to him."

00:23:24.248 --> 00:23:26.191
- Well, what did you say to him?

00:23:26.191 --> 00:23:27.556
Everyone can talk.

00:23:27.556 --> 00:23:28.716
- He'll never know.

00:23:28.716 --> 00:23:30.108
- I was like, "What did you say?"

00:23:30.108 --> 00:23:31.533
- Did he do a fuckin' Jedi mind trick?

00:23:31.533 --> 00:23:33.936
That's technically
fuckin' talkin' isn't it?

00:23:33.936 --> 00:23:35.615
- Did you like inception,
like, plant the seed?

00:23:35.615 --> 00:23:37.364
And he's just like, "It's 1500 now."

00:23:37.364 --> 00:23:39.767
- The first time I ever
saw, like, bartering happen,

00:23:39.767 --> 00:23:41.228
I was like, my mind was blown.

00:23:41.228 --> 00:23:42.061
I was like,

00:23:42.061 --> 00:23:44.409
"Wait, you can go against
the price that's written?"

00:23:44.409 --> 00:23:45.242
- You can do that?

00:23:45.242 --> 00:23:46.075
- That's an option?

00:23:46.075 --> 00:23:48.059
Because, like, we were on
a school trip to New York.

00:23:48.059 --> 00:23:49.722
It was the first time
our school ever, like,

00:23:49.722 --> 00:23:52.101
went to a different country.

00:23:52.101 --> 00:23:53.519
- You got to go to New York for school?

00:23:53.519 --> 00:23:54.352
- Yeah, dude.

00:23:54.352 --> 00:23:55.185
It was chaos.

00:23:55.185 --> 00:23:56.018
It was pure fuckin' chaos.

00:23:56.018 --> 00:23:56.851
- What the fuck?

00:23:56.851 --> 00:23:57.809
- How old were you?

00:23:57.809 --> 00:23:58.759
- 16 I think.

00:23:58.759 --> 00:23:59.717
- Oh my God.

00:23:59.717 --> 00:24:01.105
- It was an absolute mess, bro.

00:24:01.105 --> 00:24:03.308
- The only school trips I went to was

00:24:03.308 --> 00:24:05.167
just, like, France at most.

00:24:05.167 --> 00:24:07.456
That was the furthest that I've
ever gone to a school trip.

00:24:07.456 --> 00:24:08.575
- That was, like, the bougiest one.

00:24:08.575 --> 00:24:10.484
And for some reason, for one
year, they never did it again.

00:24:10.484 --> 00:24:11.820
I think they realized
it was horrible mistake.

00:24:11.820 --> 00:24:13.033
They took us to New York.

00:24:13.033 --> 00:24:14.822
It was a fuckin' mess.

00:24:14.822 --> 00:24:16.158
It was awful.

00:24:16.158 --> 00:24:18.120
I mean, if I was a teacher
there I would have hated it.

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:19.284
I had a great time.

00:24:19.284 --> 00:24:20.891
But yeah, I remember
it was very expensive,

00:24:20.891 --> 00:24:23.645
but we stayed in, like,
really fuckin' sketchy motels.

00:24:23.645 --> 00:24:25.090
I can talk about it more after the story,

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:27.361
but we were basically like,

00:24:27.361 --> 00:24:28.585
I really wanted converse

00:24:28.585 --> 00:24:30.150
'cause obviously when you're like 15, 16,

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:31.857
you see the shit on, like, American TV,

00:24:31.857 --> 00:24:32.875
you're like, "Yo, Converse."

00:24:32.875 --> 00:24:35.752
So I went to a store and
my friend was with me,

00:24:35.752 --> 00:24:37.670
and he was in the year above me.

00:24:37.670 --> 00:24:39.159
And I was like, "Man, I want to get these.

00:24:39.159 --> 00:24:40.787
"But I've only got like 30 bucks left

00:24:40.787 --> 00:24:41.638
"and they're 40 bucks."

00:24:41.638 --> 00:24:43.616
He was like, "Oh, I'll ask
him if we can do it for 30."

00:24:43.616 --> 00:24:45.778
He was like 17, bartering with him.

00:24:45.778 --> 00:24:47.192
And then eventually he said,

00:24:47.192 --> 00:24:49.746
"I'll give you for 30 if
you give me a $2 tip."

00:24:49.746 --> 00:24:51.097
And I'm like, "Is that okay?

00:24:51.097 --> 00:24:52.068
"Are you allowed to do that?"

00:24:52.068 --> 00:24:53.334
I don't know if he's the owner or what,

00:24:53.334 --> 00:24:54.692
