00:58:17.485 --> 00:58:19.073
Is VTubing part of the culture?

00:58:19.073 --> 00:58:19.923
- I think it is.

00:58:19.923 --> 00:58:23.192
I mean, it grew out of
the anime culture, right?

00:58:23.192 --> 00:58:25.541
- I mean, you know, you
gotta kind of have a like,

00:58:25.541 --> 00:58:27.060
an appreciation, for anime

00:58:27.060 --> 00:58:30.094
in order to watch anime girls streaming.

00:58:30.094 --> 00:58:31.290
- I mean, I guess.

00:58:31.290 --> 00:58:32.998
I don't know.

00:58:32.998 --> 00:58:36.897
- How deep do you say
your anime fandom goes?

00:58:36.897 --> 00:58:38.283
- That's a weird question.

00:58:38.283 --> 00:58:39.632
- Could you frame me maybe scale

00:58:39.632 --> 00:58:43.469
or something that you can judge me by?

00:58:43.469 --> 00:58:44.767
10 being a fake fan.

00:58:44.767 --> 00:58:46.625
- Okay, one is like,

00:58:46.625 --> 00:58:49.953
you know, I watch "Attack on
Titan" and "My Hero Academia."

00:58:49.953 --> 00:58:52.243
Like, just getting started level.

00:58:52.243 --> 00:58:54.824
And 10 is like, I look at an anime,

00:58:54.824 --> 00:58:57.967
and I know exactly who the
Genga artist for this is.

00:58:57.967 --> 00:58:59.126
- Fuck that.

00:58:59.126 --> 00:59:00.606
What are you on that scale?

00:59:00.606 --> 00:59:01.649
Where would you put
yourself actually then?

00:59:01.649 --> 00:59:03.065
This might help me.

00:59:03.065 --> 00:59:04.391
- Like, a seven or an eight I would say.

00:59:04.391 --> 00:59:06.776
- I would put myself
as a seven or an eight.

00:59:06.776 --> 00:59:10.368
- It probably would have been like a five,

00:59:10.368 --> 00:59:12.065
but now it's probably like a four,

00:59:12.065 --> 00:59:13.246
maybe even a three honestly.

00:59:13.246 --> 00:59:17.829
It's probably gone down to
a three, you know, recently.

00:59:18.900 --> 00:59:20.835
- Do you feel like you've
become less of an anime fan,

00:59:20.835 --> 00:59:22.416
like, more recently?

00:59:22.416 --> 00:59:23.624
And have you like falling
out with the culture

00:59:23.624 --> 00:59:25.490
ever since you moved to Japan?

00:59:25.490 --> 00:59:28.668
- I guess, I guess because...

00:59:28.668 --> 00:59:30.077
- I mean, it's not like
you don't watch anime.

00:59:30.077 --> 00:59:32.495
Like, you still keep up
to like all the stuff.

00:59:32.495 --> 00:59:34.391
- I love anime memes,
I love otaku culture,

00:59:34.391 --> 00:59:36.255
I love like the community in general.

00:59:36.255 --> 00:59:40.599
But I think just when
you get so deep into it

00:59:40.599 --> 00:59:42.610
and the community, I just start to, like,

00:59:42.610 --> 00:59:44.555
not enjoy the community
when it got into a point

00:59:44.555 --> 00:59:46.261
where it was getting really deep

00:59:46.261 --> 00:59:47.546
and everyone was like, "Name
your favorite key animator."

00:59:47.546 --> 00:59:49.262
And I was like, what, who cares?

00:59:49.262 --> 00:59:50.733
I like the show and the story.

00:59:50.733 --> 00:59:51.963
Why do I need to care about that?

00:59:51.963 --> 00:59:54.671
- I mean, we can argue that
Garnt and I are probably

00:59:54.671 --> 00:59:55.504
at that point too,

00:59:55.504 --> 00:59:56.650
but if someone came up to me and said,

00:59:56.650 --> 00:59:57.578
"Name your favorite key animator,"

00:59:57.578 --> 00:59:59.348
I'd be like, "Fuck if I know."

00:59:59.348 --> 01:00:01.385
- I think there was just a lot
of like, at least when I was,

01:00:01.385 --> 01:00:02.414
I don't know if it's still going on.

01:00:02.414 --> 01:00:03.247
I mean, you guys can tell me,

01:00:03.247 --> 01:00:05.166
but when I was trying to
get really deep into it

01:00:05.166 --> 01:00:06.924
and I really wanted to
learn more about it,

01:00:06.924 --> 01:00:08.653
it got very, like, gatekeep-y at a point.

01:00:08.653 --> 01:00:09.651
- Yeah, it definitely did.

01:00:09.651 --> 01:00:11.430
- It's been like that
for a while to be honest.

01:00:11.430 --> 01:00:14.047
- To where I just started to,
like, not really enjoy it.

01:00:14.047 --> 01:00:14.880
And then I realized,

01:00:14.880 --> 01:00:17.132
I think I just enjoy these shows way more

01:00:17.132 --> 01:00:18.263
when I'm just casual.

01:00:18.263 --> 01:00:21.498
- I mean, I just kinda
learned to appreciate it more

01:00:21.498 --> 01:00:22.599
and kind of get deeper into it

01:00:22.599 --> 01:00:26.080
without really interacting
with the community around it.

01:00:26.080 --> 01:00:27.445
- Well, I guess for a lot of people,

01:00:27.445 --> 01:00:28.653
I think me included,

01:00:28.653 --> 01:00:30.574
when I get into something the one thing

01:00:30.574 --> 01:00:32.067
that I will always do is just, like,

01:00:32.067 --> 01:00:33.774
look at the community for it and be like,

01:00:33.774 --> 01:00:34.634
all right, what's the norms?

01:00:34.634 --> 01:00:35.541
What should I get into?

01:00:35.541 --> 01:00:36.700
What's everyone saying
like the best thing?

01:00:36.700 --> 01:00:38.973
Because that's a way of
like guiding your, like,

01:00:38.973 --> 01:00:40.693
it's like a tailored experience of, like,

01:00:40.693 --> 01:00:42.798
what everyone thinks are the
best way of enjoying something.

01:00:42.798 --> 01:00:44.681
- 'Cause I feel like
you don't really follow

01:00:44.681 --> 01:00:45.806
seasonal anime anymore.

01:00:45.806 --> 01:00:48.106
You just kind of wait to see
what everyone's talking about

01:00:48.106 --> 01:00:49.320
and what's worth watching.

01:00:49.320 --> 01:00:51.226
Like, how do you decide
what anime to watch?

01:00:51.226 --> 01:00:52.963
- But I think that's because, like,

01:00:52.963 --> 01:00:55.812
the seasonal experience of viewing anime's

01:00:55.812 --> 01:00:58.375
kind of like died almost.

01:00:58.375 --> 01:00:59.490
- I don't think so.

01:00:59.490 --> 01:01:01.190
- I don't think people nearly
talk about seasonal anime

01:01:01.190 --> 01:01:04.556
in a week by week way like they used to.

01:01:04.556 --> 01:01:05.604
- I disagree.

01:01:05.604 --> 01:01:07.549
I just think it's because
last year was, like,

01:01:07.549 --> 01:01:10.004
so dry for seasonal anime

01:01:10.004 --> 01:01:12.229
that there was just nothing
for people to talk about.

01:01:12.229 --> 01:01:13.938
- It was just a lot of
mid shows last year.

01:01:13.938 --> 01:01:15.636
- I just feel like now,
especially with, like,

01:01:15.636 --> 01:01:18.347
Netflix coming and releasing
the episodes in batches.

01:01:18.347 --> 01:01:20.548
Everyone is like, it's not, you know,

01:01:20.548 --> 01:01:21.790
"Did you watch the latest
episode of Beastars?

01:01:21.790 --> 01:01:23.066
"Did you watch Beastars?"

01:01:23.066 --> 01:01:24.792
- But, like, that's like one

01:01:24.792 --> 01:01:27.421
out of every fuckin' 100 anime
that comes out every year.

01:01:27.421 --> 01:01:29.134
- I feel like everyone asks that now.

01:01:29.134 --> 01:01:30.818
It's not, "Did you watch
the newest episode?"

01:01:30.818 --> 01:01:32.498
It's "Are you watching Attack on Titan?"

01:01:32.498 --> 01:01:34.956
- I would say like,
people are still asking,

01:01:34.956 --> 01:01:37.025
"Are you watching the newest
episode of Attack on Titan?"

01:01:37.025 --> 01:01:38.754
- People just say "Are you
watching Attack on Titan?"

01:01:38.754 --> 01:01:40.290
Not, "Are you watching
the newest episode?"

01:01:40.290 --> 01:01:43.901
- Literally every stream
I do, there's always,

01:01:43.901 --> 01:01:45.346
it's like, "Have you watched this anime?"

01:01:45.346 --> 01:01:46.330
- "Attack on Titan" is different.

01:01:46.330 --> 01:01:47.198
"Attack on Titan" is like-

01:01:47.198 --> 01:01:48.503
- No, not "Attack on Titan."

01:01:48.503 --> 01:01:49.476
Like, any seasonal anime.

01:01:49.476 --> 01:01:51.877
- No, normally I never get
seasonal anime people asking me.

01:01:51.877 --> 01:01:53.255
- Oh, I get that all the time.

01:01:53.255 --> 01:01:55.128
- No one gives a fuck
if I was watching, like,

01:01:55.128 --> 01:01:57.286
Oriomon, what is that called?

01:01:57.286 --> 01:01:58.324
What the fuck is it called?

01:01:58.324 --> 01:01:59.157
What's it called?

01:01:59.157 --> 01:01:59.990
- "Oreimo."

01:01:59.990 --> 01:02:00.823
- That's it.

01:02:00.823 --> 01:02:01.656
Who the fuck gives a shit?

01:02:01.656 --> 01:02:03.227
- Were you trying to say
"Oreimo" and "Doraemon?"

01:02:03.227 --> 01:02:04.992
- Yeah, who gives a shit?

01:02:04.992 --> 01:02:05.831
- That's cursed.

01:02:05.831 --> 01:02:09.380
- Generic feels good anime
that's an eight season, you know,

01:02:09.380 --> 01:02:10.683
like, are you watching that?

01:02:10.683 --> 01:02:12.941
No one asks me fuck if
I'm watching that shit.

01:02:12.941 --> 01:02:14.644
No one asks me if I watch "Deca-Dence."

01:02:14.644 --> 01:02:15.481
You know what I fuckin' mean?

01:02:15.481 --> 01:02:16.873
Like, no one gives a shit

01:02:16.873 --> 01:02:18.302
'cause there's so many
animes that are so mid now

01:02:18.302 --> 01:02:19.393
and there's so many coming out.

01:02:19.393 --> 01:02:20.534
- God, I remember "Deca-Dence."

01:02:20.534 --> 01:02:21.406
I tried watching that.

01:02:21.406 --> 01:02:22.827
- There's so many animes
that are coming out

01:02:22.827 --> 01:02:25.071
that the only ones people,
I seem to have that,

01:02:25.071 --> 01:02:26.379
because it used to be,

01:02:26.379 --> 01:02:28.074
again when there's a
lot less anime as well,

01:02:28.074 --> 01:02:29.186
that everyone could kind of ask

01:02:29.186 --> 01:02:30.512
are you watching these shows?

01:02:30.512 --> 01:02:31.345
Are you watching it weekly?

01:02:31.345 --> 01:02:32.873
And now there's just so fuckin' many.

01:02:32.873 --> 01:02:34.666
And we have so many like good shows

01:02:34.666 --> 01:02:35.994
but like we only really,

01:02:35.994 --> 01:02:37.492
I find in my experience at general,

01:02:37.492 --> 01:02:39.236
Twitter only really asked

01:02:39.236 --> 01:02:40.183
if you're watching a show weekly now

01:02:40.183 --> 01:02:41.268
or keeps up with the hype,

01:02:41.268 --> 01:02:43.118
if it's a big event
like "Attack on Titan."

01:02:43.118 --> 01:02:44.039
- Right, right, right.

01:02:44.039 --> 01:02:45.710
'Cause I feel it was missing last year was

01:02:45.710 --> 01:02:47.165
that fuckin' big event.

01:02:47.165 --> 01:02:48.902
'Cause last year we had something
like the "Demon Slayer,"

01:02:48.902 --> 01:02:51.244
that "Demon Slayer"
episode that really like-

01:02:51.244 --> 01:02:53.639
- But even then I never saw,
like, week by week plays

01:02:53.639 --> 01:02:54.892
by "Demon Slayer."

01:02:54.892 --> 01:02:55.893
- Week by week plays.

01:02:55.893 --> 01:02:57.028
(Garnt laughs)

01:02:57.028 --> 01:02:58.718
- "Yo, Demon Slayer episode 17!

01:02:58.718 --> 01:03:00.132
"Boys, what we all sayin' on Twitter?"

01:03:00.132 --> 01:03:01.414
You know, there wasn't like any of that.

01:03:01.414 --> 01:03:02.974
It was just episode 19 was amazing.

01:03:02.974 --> 01:03:04.652
It gave the birth of my children.

01:03:04.652 --> 01:03:05.916
Jesus Christ is re reborn.

01:03:05.916 --> 01:03:07.521
Like that's what happened.

01:03:07.521 --> 01:03:08.366
That was it.

01:03:08.366 --> 01:03:09.415
Like, there wasn't anything else

01:03:09.415 --> 01:03:11.556
other than like, "Demon Slayer good."

01:03:11.556 --> 01:03:12.556
That was it.

01:03:13.634 --> 01:03:16.081
Do you not think that's kind
of like, it shifted a little?

01:03:16.081 --> 01:03:18.742
Am I seeing something you guys aren't?

01:03:18.742 --> 01:03:20.849
- I think maybe it's just shifted

01:03:20.849 --> 01:03:22.931
just because you've kind
of shifted away from it.

01:03:22.931 --> 01:03:24.652
'Cause I've also shifted away from it too.

01:03:24.652 --> 01:03:27.072
And I've definitely
noticed like the lack of-

01:03:27.072 --> 01:03:29.655
- I do feel like that's so many people

01:03:29.655 --> 01:03:31.825
'cause I know so many
people now who, like,

01:03:31.825 --> 01:03:33.522
they say they're anime fans-

01:03:33.522 --> 01:03:35.516
- It shifted to manga, 100%.

01:03:35.516 --> 01:03:39.466
- And all they do is read
manga, watch VTubers,

01:03:39.466 --> 01:03:41.157
and play gacha games.

01:03:41.157 --> 01:03:43.319
- Wow, I'm in this photo and I hate it.

01:03:43.319 --> 01:03:45.197
(everyone laughs)

01:03:45.197 --> 01:03:46.389
That's literally me!

01:03:46.389 --> 01:03:48.320
That was me in 2020.

01:03:48.320 --> 01:03:50.918
- I never see people talk
about "episode three of this."

01:03:50.918 --> 01:03:52.713
It's always "chapter this of this manga."

01:03:52.713 --> 01:03:54.686
'Cause everyone knows that
they're released at this point.

01:03:54.686 --> 01:03:56.126
And then everyone keeps
up with it on Twitter.

01:03:56.126 --> 01:03:58.628
But I never see it for anime.

01:03:58.628 --> 01:04:00.572
No one does anime episode reviews anymore

01:04:00.572 --> 01:04:02.639
except for like big shows
like "Attack on Titan."

01:04:02.639 --> 01:04:04.674
Everyone does manga chapter things still.

01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:06.278
They're so popular.

01:04:06.278 --> 01:04:07.857
I genuinely think it's shifted.

01:04:07.857 --> 01:04:09.307
I don't think I'm the weird one here.

01:04:09.307 --> 01:04:10.779
I think you guys can't see the truth.

01:04:10.779 --> 01:04:12.237
What's happening?

01:04:12.237 --> 01:04:13.429
- I disagree with, like,

01:04:13.429 --> 01:04:14.837
"no one does episode reviews anymore."

01:04:14.837 --> 01:04:15.670
- Not really.

01:04:15.670 --> 01:04:17.563
- 'Cause there's still like
a big group of YouTubers

01:04:17.563 --> 01:04:18.396
who still do it.

01:04:18.396 --> 01:04:19.229
- Oh really?

01:04:19.229 --> 01:04:20.062
You watch episode reviews?

01:04:20.062 --> 01:04:21.141
Name every episode reviewer right now.

01:04:21.141 --> 01:04:22.349
- Chibi.

01:04:22.349 --> 01:04:23.927
- Chibi's probably the only person I know.

01:04:23.927 --> 01:04:25.513
- Chibi's the only one.

01:04:25.513 --> 01:04:26.473
- YouTube will be taken down

01:04:26.473 --> 01:04:27.713
and Chibi will still be making reviews.

01:04:27.713 --> 01:04:31.276
I don't know who like, come
on, that doesn't count, man.

01:04:31.276 --> 01:04:33.449
- That's the only one that
matters in my opinion.

01:04:33.449 --> 01:04:34.839
- I guess, I mean-

01:04:34.839 --> 01:04:39.576
- I feel like that kind
of mirrors the culture now

01:04:39.576 --> 01:04:42.544
because I feel like definitely
being an anime YouTuber

01:04:42.544 --> 01:04:44.794
last year was fuckin' hard.

01:04:45.778 --> 01:04:48.611
Anime content last year was, like,

01:04:49.510 --> 01:04:50.635
from my perspective,

01:04:50.635 --> 01:04:52.614
anime content on YouTube
just didn't do as well.

01:04:52.614 --> 01:04:53.785
'Cause no one was watching any anime.

01:04:53.785 --> 01:04:56.326
But videos around anime culture,

01:04:56.326 --> 01:04:57.495
like what you guys were doing,

01:04:57.495 --> 01:05:01.186
you guys fuckin' killed it
last year, in my opinion.

01:05:01.186 --> 01:05:04.001
And I feel like that's because, like,

01:05:04.001 --> 01:05:06.122
people care less about
individual shows now.

01:05:06.122 --> 01:05:07.943
And people just more
care about the culture.

01:05:07.943 --> 01:05:10.951
- I think the last time
I did a show or a video

01:05:10.951 --> 01:05:12.668
on a show that was like seasonal

01:05:12.668 --> 01:05:15.341
and ongoing was fuckin'
"Promised Neverland."

01:05:15.341 --> 01:05:17.151
And that was what, two years?

01:05:17.151 --> 01:05:18.174
Three years ago almost.

01:05:18.174 --> 01:05:19.131
- I think mine's like "Banana Fish."

01:05:19.131 --> 01:05:20.191
It's fuckin' amazing.

01:05:20.191 --> 01:05:21.953
- It was like two or
three years ago, right?

01:05:21.953 --> 01:05:23.074
And it's like, since then,

01:05:23.074 --> 01:05:25.026
it's just like every season comes around

01:05:25.026 --> 01:05:26.289
and I do a what will I be watching?

01:05:26.289 --> 01:05:27.615
And then I look at the
list and I was like-

01:05:27.615 --> 01:05:29.382
- The biggest lie of the century.

01:05:29.382 --> 01:05:31.274
- Joey needs to change the title to

01:05:31.274 --> 01:05:32.694
"I Lied to You For 20 Minutes Straight."

01:05:32.694 --> 01:05:33.989
(everyone laughs)

01:05:33.989 --> 01:05:36.259
- "What I'm Looking At."

01:05:36.259 --> 01:05:38.072
- I love how the comments
have finally called you out

01:05:38.072 --> 01:05:38.905
on it though.

01:05:38.905 --> 01:05:40.042
They're like, "Don't fucking lie to us."

01:05:40.042 --> 01:05:40.875
- Yeah, of course.

01:05:40.875 --> 01:05:43.866
No, that series now is just
a fuckin' quick easy way

01:05:43.866 --> 01:05:45.842
of being like, "Oh, let's see
what Joey thinks about this.

01:05:45.842 --> 01:05:47.521
"We know he's not gonna watch it,

01:05:47.521 --> 01:05:49.493
"but at least we'll know
what he feels about it."

01:05:49.493 --> 01:05:51.879
- For me, seasonal anime has just become

01:05:51.879 --> 01:05:53.888
this glorified manga
recommendation system.

01:05:53.888 --> 01:05:54.921
(Connor laughs)

01:05:54.921 --> 01:05:59.167
Where if I find a series
like this, it's so rare-

01:05:59.167 --> 01:06:01.093
- This is what, like,
shopping is to Amazon.

01:06:01.093 --> 01:06:03.080
I go to the store to go
and buy it on Amazon.

01:06:03.080 --> 01:06:04.750
(everyone laughs)

01:06:04.750 --> 01:06:08.083
- 'Cause most of the
time you find an anime

01:06:08.083 --> 01:06:10.085
and it's like, we talked
about this before,

01:06:10.085 --> 01:06:13.752
where it's not an
adaptation that's amazing.

01:06:14.694 --> 01:06:17.541
It's a passible adaptation
where I'm just, like,

01:06:17.541 --> 01:06:18.845
I don't get anything more than this

01:06:18.845 --> 01:06:21.275
from, like, watching the anime
versus reading the manga.

01:06:21.275 --> 01:06:23.599
So you just end up reading the manga.

01:06:23.599 --> 01:06:26.755
"Jujutsu Kaisen" is like
one of the few, like,

01:06:26.755 --> 01:06:27.870
"Jujutsu Kaisen," "Jojo,"

01:06:27.870 --> 01:06:30.113
and like some of like
the big shonen ones are

01:06:30.113 --> 01:06:33.174
one of the few exceptions
where they actually have budget

01:06:33.174 --> 01:06:34.709
and money behind this to make this

01:06:34.709 --> 01:06:36.713
a fuckin' amazing production.

01:06:36.713 --> 01:06:37.579
You know what I mean?

01:06:37.579 --> 01:06:39.917
But for the most part
you have a production

01:06:39.917 --> 01:06:41.625
that's just mediocre.

01:06:41.625 --> 01:06:42.458
It's okay.

01:06:42.458 --> 01:06:43.291
- They're just there.

01:06:43.291 --> 01:06:44.428
- They're just there, and it's just like,

01:06:44.428 --> 01:06:46.208
I'd rather just read
